inance at 100%+ debt/GDP with eroding convenience yields. The offsetting force is decisive and is why I do not go higher: the MODAL large drawdown in this window is an AI-capex bust (locked 66% prior), and an AI capex bust is DISINFLATIONARY, so the bid works precisely in the most likely scenario.\n\nCORRELATION: strongly positive between A and B — both are \"rates are the shock\" worlds. P(B1|A) = 0.88; P(B2|B1,A) = 0.58; P(B|A) = 0.51. JOINT = 0.32 x 0.51 = 0.163 -> 16. Most forecasters will over-rate this conjunction because each leg individually feels live; the binding constraint is that a 10-year MOVE mean of 105 is above every decade average on record except 1987-94 and 2022-24.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:59.250Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"Atlanta Fed Wage Growth Tracker, 12-month moving average of median hourly wage growth: the Construction-and-Mining series MINUS the Finance-and-Business-Services series. Current observed state is a dead heat on the closest available proxies (Education and Health 4.2 in Sep-2025; Finance and Business Services 4.2 in Feb-2026; Construction and Mining latest value unverified at my horizon). Watch for a gap exceeding +1.5pp sustained across four consecutive quarters. Caveat: these are broad industry groups, not ISIC F/Q/J/K/M, and they are unweighted medians.\",\"by_when\":\"Q4 2029\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"CQ1 rises from 12 to roughly 25-30 (the second conjunct's marginal goes from 16% to ~40%); hypothesis plank (a) rises from 7 to ~25; CQ6-B gains ~4 points from C and D. If instead the gap is still under +0.5pp by Q4 2029, CQ1 falls to ~7 and plank (a) to ~4.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Realized 2027 hyperscaler capex versus the Oct-2026 guidance, together with disclosed AI-asset impairments or cancelled buildouts in 10-K/20-F filings. Observed baseline: